  "_comment": "WIMP-nucleon SI exclusion-limit reproduction, DAMIC 0.6 kg-day (PhysRevD.94.082006 / arXiv:1607.07410), Fig. 11 -- SINGLE-CHANNEL 1x1-only version, WITH the low-energy-excess (LEE) background enabled (damic_snolab_2023_skipper preset, arXiv:2306.01717). Identical to wimp_damic_snolab_2016.json except for backgrounds.lee. WHY 1x1-only, not joint: an earlier joint (response.channels[]) version of this comparison produced BIT-IDENTICAL upper limits to its baseline sibling across all 28 mass points -- traced to RunJointChannelScan (apps/ccdarksens_scan_generic.cc) never checking cfg.backgrounds().has_lee_bkg at all (only the single-channel MakeBackground() path in BackgroundFactory.cc does). Per explicit instruction, scope reduced to 1x1-only for now, which correctly applies the LEE term via the already-working single-channel path (verified: this config's upper limits differ from the baseline's at every mass point once the LEE preset's exponential rate is added). A joint-channel LEE fix is a known follow-up, not done here.",
  "_header": "Diego Venegas-Vargas | DAMIC-M collaboration | CCDarkSens Framework -- Student example: WIMP-nucleon SI, DAMIC at SNOLAB (2016) reproduction, single-channel (1x1 only) cluster-energy likelihood, WITH the low-energy-excess (LEE) background enabled (damic_snolab_2023_skipper preset, arXiv:2306.01717). First working on/off comparison for this feature -- see _comment for the joint-path bug this scope change sidesteps."
}
